TIKI
// HZM coop [user 2026-09-06, bug-2508] HIGGINS STERN WAKE TRAIL - the m3l1a run-in (ocean_2026-09-06 item 3).
//
// A carrier on the coop_bloodcloud / coop_uwbubble skeleton (invisible dummy2.skd + effectentity + notsolid
// + rendereffects +dontdraw, which still SENDS the entity so the client block runs, fgame/entity.cpp:881)
// whose one block is Spearhead's `models/emitters/waterWake.tik` originemitter (mainta/pak1.pk3), the
// retail recipe for a wake trailing a moving boat: flat oriented sprites, spawnrate 1, life 15, scalerate
// 0.7, fade. An originemitter is the one block kind a script_model carrier renders (bug-2477 - every `sfx`
// block returns at once from StartSFXCommand on a script-spawned entity).
//
// SPRITE: `waterWake.spr` strips to shader `waterWake`, defined IDENTICALLY in mainta/pak1.pk3 and
// maintt/pak1.pk3 scripts/effects.shader (spriteGen oriented, clampmap textures/fx/water/waterWake.tga,
// blendfunc blend, rgbGen vertex, sort nearest); both paks mount under com_target_game 2, the mod ships no
// scripts/effects.shader of its own (whole-file override checked 2026-09-06), and the texture is in
// mainta/pak1 as waterWake.tga + waterwake.dds. Retail never needs `emitteron` for this: an emitter is
// active from the first frame unless its block says `startoff` (cg_commands.h emitterthing_t::GetEmitTime).
// Retail's own tik toggled it through an `anim start` notetrack, which a script carrier never plays.
//
// RATE IS AUTHORED FOR cg_effectdetail 1 (coop_defaults.cfg:13), the shipped value, as bug-2507 taught:
// the emitter loop multiplies by cg_effectdetail directly (cg_commands.cpp:5010), so spawnrate 1 IS one
// sprite per second here and life 15 keeps ~15 alive - the "~15 flat sprites" trail of the design. At the
// engine's 0.2 default it would be three.
//
// ONE DEPARTURE FROM SPEARHEAD: `accel -5 0 0` became `accel 0 -5 0`. accel is world-space (the same
// field gravity uses) and Spearhead's rowboat travelled along X; the Higgins fleet runs `movenorth`, +Y,
// so the sprites drift astern (south) instead of sideways across the lane.
//
// NO wateronly: the sprites sit ON the -520 surface plane, where CM_PointContents is not reliably water,
// and wateronly would cull them on their first tick (the bug-2359 lesson, the other way round).
// PLACEMENT (script side, level.coop_wakeOn): park the carrier at the stern at the water surface
// (coopified.scr coop_waterZ), not at the hull origin -563.7; no `offset` is authored here on purpose.
setup
{
	scale 1.0
	path models/fx/dummy
	skelmodel dummy2.skd
}

init
{
	server
	{
		classname effectentity
		notsolid
		rendereffects +dontdraw
	}
	client
	{
		cache waterWake.spr

		// Spearhead's waterWake.tik block, verbatim except the accel axis (see above).
		originemitter coop_wwake
		(
			spawnrate 1
			model waterWake.spr
			alpha 0.7
			life 15
			scalerate 0.7
			accel 0 -5 0
			angles 90 0 crandom 180
			avelocity 0 0 crandom 40
			scalemin 0.3
			scalemax 0.5
			fade
		)
	}
}

animations
{
	// Both point at the same clip. `start` exists so a caller's `anim start` is a real animation.
	idle  dummy2.skc
	start dummy2.skc
}
